      "content": "If you use the chair specifically for business purposes (in your home studio) more than 50% of the time, you can directly deduct the full cost as a business expense. If the business use is less than 50%, you can only deduct the business use percentage, but it's still recommended to keep records of the hours used for work and your home office setup. For receipts, consider setting up a digital system, like an envelope or app, to organize and track your expenses as you incur them.",
